    "description": "During this time I developed both Windows applications and web-based software using Microsoft .NET (VB & C#) and Microsoft SQL.  Working initially as part of a small team, and ultimately as the sole developer, I was responsible for the entire life-cycle of the project from design right through to support,  and implemented several large-scale projects which utilized SQL and SSRS to centralize data management.  Some of these are:-\n\n* Home-buyer Selection System:-\nComplete client/server system which can be deployed across many design centers, saving on maintenance costs and time. Automatically calculated pricing from 'Builder specific' product and price lists enabling accurate and timely quotes. Electronically generated orders, complete with installation diagrams, for interfacing with ACCPAC ERP, reducing the need for order entry staff and increasing accuracy of material purchasing and installation.\n\n* Product Management:-\nCentral Product database for all materials purchased and installed, complete with customizable price lists and product lists for each customer. Extensive custom reporting to show most profitable products, with ability to place products into pricing groups based on desired profit margin. Created interface between product database and ACCPAC ERP to automatically synchronize product details, allowing for accurate inventory and sales job cost reporting.\n\n* Special Achievements\nReceived ‘Outstanding Achievement Awards’ for years 2003-2007 (awards discontinued after 2007) \nExtensively customized ACCPAC ERP using .NET, SQL and Crystal Reports in order to add missing functionality specific to the new-home industry, including several custom user interfaces.  Integrated package with current systems and data.",
